[38;2;124;124;124mThe question: Is $V_k$ a transitive model of ZFC?[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mYes, this is a classical result. Let me justify it.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Transitivity**: $V_k$ is always transitive for any limit ordinal $k$, since [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$V_\alpha$ is transitive for every ordinal $\alpha$. Actually, $V_\alpha$ is [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mtransitive for all ordinals $\alpha$. If $x \in V_\alpha$, then $x \in V_\beta$ [0m[38;2;124;124;124mfor some $\beta < \alpha$, and $V_\beta \subseteq V_\alpha$ when $\beta < [0m
